{"type":"message","id":"2c5aeca1","parentId":"72ace1f2","timestamp":"2026-02-19T11:47:33.790Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_1vx5n6pmjxop_3","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Secrets Detection Rules\n- id: S001\n  title: Hardcoded API Key/Token\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:api[_-]?key|access[_-]?token|auth[_-]?token|bearer[_-]?token)[\"''\\s]*[=:][\"''\\s]*([a-z0-9_-]{20,})'\n  severity: critical\n  recommendation: Use environment variables or secure credential storage instead\n- id: S002\n  title: Hardcoded Password\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:password|passwd|pwd)[\"''\\s]*[=:][\"''\\s]*([^\"\\n''\\s]{8,})'\n  severity: critical\n  recommendation: Use environment variables or secure credential storage instead\n- id: S003\n  title: Private Key Exposure Risk\n  pattern: '-----BEGIN[ A-Z]* PRIVATE KEY-----'\n  severity: critical\n  recommendation: Never store private keys in source code\n- id: S004\n  title: Base64 Encoded Secret\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:secret|key|token)[\"''\\s]*[=:][\"''\\s]*([a-z0-9+/]{20,}={0,2})'\n  severity: high\n  recommendation: Avoid storing encoded secrets in source code\n- id: S005\n  title: Cloud Provider Credentials Pattern\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:aws[_-]?access[_-]?key|azure[_-]?subscription|gcp[_-]?service[_-]?account)'\n  severity: critical\n  recommendation: Use IAM roles or managed identity instead of hardcoded credentials"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771501653779}}
{"type":"message","id":"6dbf1192","parentId":"2c5aeca1","timestamp":"2026-02-19T11:47:58.447Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the structure:\n1. The scanner.js loads rules from the rules/ directory\n2. Rules are YAML files with patterns, severity, etc.\n3. I need to add web.yaml and crypto.yaml\n\nLet me also check the existing audit.sh to understand the full setup:","thinkingSignature":"50b57207e51922f2bc722aa10b81161302acc50e1a2f4e470512607e69634aeb"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_01240ktwal0w_1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/ecs-user/.openclaw/workspace/skills/skill-audit/scripts/audit.sh"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-cn","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":3882,"output":103,"cacheRead":10439,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":14424,"cost":{"input":0.058230000000000004,"output":0.00618,"cacheRead":0.020878,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.085288}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771501653790}}
{"type":"message","id":"862fcdca","parentId":"6dbf1192","timestamp":"2026-02-19T11:47:58.487Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_01240ktwal0w_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/bin/bash\n\n# Skill Audit - Main Entry Point\n# Usage: skill-audit [options] [path]\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# Default values\nTARGET_PATH=\"\"\nOUTPUT_FILE=\"\"\nVERBOSE=false\nRULE_TYPES=\"\"\n\n# Print usage\nprint_usage() {\n  cat << EOF\nUsage: skill-audit [options] [path]\n\nOptions:\n  -t, --type TYPES    Comma-separated rule types (secrets,commands,files,network,permissions)\n  -o, --output FILE   Output JSON report to file\n  -v, --verbose       Verbose output with code snippets\n  -h, --help          Show this help message\n\nExamples:\n  skill-audit                           # Audit all skills in workspace\n  skill-audit /path/to/skill           # Audit specific skill\n  skill-audit --type secrets,commands  # Audit specific rule types\n  skill-audit --output report.json     # Save report to file\nEOF\n}\n\n# Parse arguments\nwhile [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do\n  case $1 in\n    -t|--type)\n      RULE_TYPES=\"$2\"\n      shift 2\n      ;;\n    -o|--output)\n      OUTPUT_FILE=\"$2\"\n      shift 2\n      ;;\n    -v|--verbose)\n      VERBOSE=true\n      shift\n      ;;\n    -h|--help)\n      print_usage\n      exit 0\n      ;;\n    -*)\n      echo \"Unknown option $1\"\n      print_usage\n      exit 1\n      ;;\n    *)\n      TARGET_PATH=\"$1\"\n      shift\n      ;;\n  esac\ndone\n\n# Determine target path\nif [ -z \"$TARGET_PATH\" ]; then\n  # Try to find skills directory in common locations\n  if [ -d \"./skills\" ]; then\n    TARGET_PATH=\"./skills\"\n  elif [ -d \"../skills\" ]; then\n    TARGET_PATH=\"../skills\"\n  else\n    echo \"Error: No target path specified and no skills directory found\"\n    exit 1\n  fi\nfi\n\n# Validate target path\nif [ ! -e \"$TARGET_PATH\" ]; then\n  echo \"Error: Target path does not exist: $TARGET_PATH\"\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# Resolve symlinks\nREAL_TARGET=$(realpath \"$TARGET_PATH\")\n\n# Prepare arguments for scanner\nARGS=()\n[ -n \"$RULE_TYPES\" ] && ARGS+=(\"--types\" \"$RULE_TYPES\")\n[ \"$VERBOSE\" = true ] && ARGS+=(\"--verbose\")\nARGS+=(\"$REAL_TARGET\")\n\n# Run scanner and capture output\nif [ -n \"$OUTPUT_FILE\" ]; then\n  node \"$(dirname \"$0\")/scanner.js\" \"${ARGS[@]}\" > \"$OUTPUT_FILE\"\n  echo \"Report saved to $OUTPUT_FILE\"\nelse\n  node \"$(dirname \"$0\")/scanner.js\" \"${ARGS[@]}\"\nfi"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771501678468}}
{"type":"message","id":"d99bb61b","parentId":"862fcdca","timestamp":"2026-02-19T11:48:42.248Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a full understanding of the structure. Let me:\n\n1. Create web.yaml with Web security rules (SQL injection, XSS, etc.)\n2. Create crypto.yaml with cryptocurrency related rules\n3. Update scanner.js to support the new rule types (web, crypto)\n4. Create quick-audit.sh as a quick scanning script\n\nLet me create the new files:","thinkingSignature":"86dd45913004d679bc76d1ec79e4c9557a0b537ef585685c9adef5bd04cf9b89"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create the new rule files and update the scanner. Let me start:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_6mpl94c4be5n_1","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# Web Security Rules\n# Detects common web security vulnerabilities\n\n- id: W001\n  title: SQL Injection Risk\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:select|insert|update|delete|drop|create|alter)\\s+.*\\+.*[\"\\']'\n  severity: critical\n  recommendation: Use parameterized queries or prepared statements instead of string concatenation\n\n- id: W002\n  title: Unsanitized Input in SQL Query\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:execute|query|exec)\\s*\\(\\s*[\"\\'].*\\$\\{?'\n  severity: critical\n  recommendation: Sanitize inputs or use ORM/parameterized queries\n\n- id: W003\n  title: Potential XSS - innerHTML Assignment\n  pattern: '(?:\\.innerHTML|\\.outerHTML|insertAdjacentHTML)\\s*=\\s*[^;]+'\n  severity: high\n  recommendation: Use textContent instead of innerHTML, or sanitize with DOMPurify\n\n- id: W004\n  title: Unsanitized eval() Usage\n  pattern: '\\beval\\s*\\([^)]*\\$'\n  severity: critical\n  recommendation: Avoid eval() with user input; use safer alternatives\n\n- id: W005\n  title: Unsafe DOM Manipulation with User Input\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:document\\.write|dynDocumentWrite)\\s*\\('\n  severity: high\n  recommendation: Use safer DOM manipulation methods like textContent\n\n- id: W006\n  title: Missing Content Security Policy Header\n  pattern: 'Content-Security-Policy'\n  severity: medium\n  recommendation: Add CSP headers to protect against XSS and data injection\n\n- id: W007\n  title: Insecure Random Number Generation\n  pattern: 'Math\\.random\\s*\\('\n  severity: medium\n  recommendation: Use crypto.getRandomValues() for security-sensitive randomness\n\n- id: W008\n  title: Disabled SSL/TLS Verification\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:rejectUnauthorized|verify|ssl:\\s*false|secure:\\s*false)'\n  severity: critical\n  recommendation: Always verify SSL certificates in production\n\n- id: W009\n  title: Weak Cryptographic Algorithm\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:md5|sha1|des|rc4)\\s*\\('\n  severity: high\n  recommendation: Use SHA-256 or stronger algorithms\n\n- id: W010\n  title: Path Traversal Risk\n  pattern: '(?:\\.\\./|\\.\\.\\\\\\\\|%2e%2e)'\n  severity: high\n  recommendation: Validate and sanitize file path inputs\n\n- id: W011\n  title: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) Risk\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:fetch|axios|request|http\\.get|http\\.post).*\\$\\{?'\n  severity: high\n  description: URL parameters should be validated against allowlists\n  recommendation: Validate URLs against allowlists and avoid user-controlled URL parameters\n\n- id: W012\n  title: Insecure XML Parser Configuration\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:DOMParser|XMLHttpRequest).*dangerouslySetInnerHTML'\n  severity: high\n  recommendation: Disable external entity processing in XML parsers\n\n- id: W013\n  title: Missing HTTP Security Headers\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:X-Frame-Options|X-Content-Type-Options|X-XSS-Protection)'\n  severity: medium\n  recommendation: Add security headers: X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options, Strict-Transport-Security\n\n- id: W014\n  title: Cookie Without Secure Flag\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:cookie|setCookie).*[\"\\'][^\"\\']*[\"\\'].*secure:\\s*false'\n  severity: medium\n  recommendation: Always set the Secure flag for cookies in production\n","file_path":"/home/ecs-user/.openclaw/workspace/skills/skill-audit/scripts/rules/web.yaml"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_6mpl94c4be5n_2","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# Cryptocurrency & Blockchain Security Rules\n# Detects crypto-related security risks\n\n- id: C001\n  title: Hardcoded Cryptocurrency Private Key\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:private[_-]?key|crypto[_-]?wallet).*[\"\\'][a-f0-9]{64}[\"\\']'\n  severity: critical\n  recommendation: Never store private keys in source code; use secure key management\n\n- id: C002\n  title: Cryptocurrency Address Exposure\n  pattern: '(?:bc1|[13])[a-zA-HJ-NP-Z0-9]{25,39}'\n  severity: high\n  recommendation: Avoid hardcoding cryptocurrency addresses in source code\n\n- id: C003\n  title: Suspicious Cryptocurrency Mining Pattern\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:coinhive|coin-hive|cryptonight|webminer|miner\\.start)'\n  severity: critical\n  description: Potential cryptojacking detection\n  recommendation: Remove any cryptomining code from web applications\n\n- id: C004\n  title: Wallet Connection with Insecure RPC\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:web3|http://).*(?:wallet|metamask|infura)'\n  severity: medium\n  recommendation: Use secure HTTPS endpoints for blockchain RPC connections\n\n- id: C005\n  title: Hardcoded API Endpoint for Blockchain\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:etherscan|infura|alchemy).*(?:api[_-]?key|url)'\n  severity: critical\n  recommendation: Use environment variables for API keys; never commit to source\n\n- id: C006\n  title: Missing Transaction Validation\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:sendTransaction|transfer|submitTransaction).*\\.then'\n  severity: medium\n  description: Transaction sent without proper validation\n  recommendation: Always validate transaction parameters before signing\n\n- id: C007\n  title: Insecure Smart Contract Interaction\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:contract\\.methods|contract\\.call).*\\{.*gas'\n  severity: medium\n  recommendation: Specify appropriate gas limits and use Safe functions\n\n- id: C008\n  title: Exposed Mnemonic Phrase\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:mnemonic|seed[_-]?phrase|bip39).*[\"\\'][a-z ]+[\"\\']'\n  severity: critical\n  recommendation: Never store mnemonic phrases in source code\n\n- id: C009\n  title: Weak Random for Crypto Operations\n  pattern: '(?i)Math\\.random.*crypto|random.*wallet'\n  severity: high\n  recommendation: Use crypto.getRandomValues() or proper CSPRNG for wallet generation\n\n- id: C010\n  title: Unsigned Blockchain Transaction\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:sign|signTransaction|sendRawTransaction)'\n  severity: medium\n  recommendation: Always sign transactions before broadcasting to blockchain\n\n- id: C011\n  title: Missing Chain ID Specification\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:chainId|networkId).*[!=]=.*\\d+'\n  severity: medium\n  recommendation: Always specify chain ID to prevent replay attacks\n\n- id: C012\n  title: Trusting Block Number for Timing\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:block\\.number|blockTimestamp|Date\\.now\\(\\))'\n  severity: low\n  description: Using block numbers or timestamps for critical timing\n  recommendation: Consider using Chainlink oracles for time-sensitive operations\n\n- id: C013\n  title: Deprecated Ethereum API Usage\n  pattern: '(?i)(?:web3\\.sha3|web3\\.soliditySha3|eth\\.sign)'\n  severity: medium\n  recommendation: Use updated API methods; eth_sign is deprecated\n","file_path":"/home/ecs-user/.openclaw/workspace/skills/skill-audit/scripts/rules/crypto.yaml"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-cn","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":4602,"output":1803,"cacheRead":10439,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":16844,"cost":{"input":0.06903000000000001,"output":0.10818,"cacheRead":0.020878,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.19808800000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771501678487}}
